cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "sharedstat: Diagnose and Correct Statistics Built from a Shared Component"
# This tree is version 0.1.2. A version DOI is minted after the GitHub Release, so it is not in this file; take it
# from the Zenodo record for v0.1.2. The DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22693748 is v0.1.0’s, which exports eleven functions
# and lacks the two reliability functions added here. Cite the version you used.
version: 0.1.2
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ruichen-bioinfo/sharedstat"
# No date-released. The field means the date this version was released, and 0.1.2 has not been. It briefly said
# 2026-09-23, which was the date the file was edited, not a release date. Add it in the same change that adds the DOI.
abstract: >-
  Quantifies and corrects bias in statistics built from a shared measured component. Covers four
  constructions: a statistic formed against a shared reference arm, a residual correlated with the
  component subtracted from it, a count of significant features read as an ordering of effect sizes,
  and an interaction contrast on compositional counts. Provides two estimators, the attenuation
  result, the five admission checks and a known-truth simulator in which compositionality emerges
  from closed-sum sampling rather than being imposed.
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Rui
    affiliation: Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München
keywords:
  - spurious correlation
  - shared component
  - measurement error
  - regression dilution
  - mathematical coupling
  - instrumental variable
  - compositional data
  - regulatory divergence
  - RNA-seq
  - reproducibility
